From: Austin Schuh <austin.linux@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:30:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] clocksource: timer-tegra186: request the IRQ after creating
 the WDT

"NVIDIA: SAUCE: clocksource: timer-tegra186: Enable WDT at probe"
requests the timer's IRQ before it creates the watchdog, and the handler
dereferences tegra->wdt.  After a kexec, the previous kernel leaves the
watchdog running with its interrupt pending, so the handler runs as soon
as the IRQ is requested, with tegra->wdt still NULL:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000000000000c0
  pc : tegra186_timer_irq+0x1c/0x60
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Oops: Fatal exception in interrupt

and MB1 resets the board.  Every kexec on the Orin Nano has ended that
way.  Create the watchdog first, as mainline has since "clocksource/
drivers/timer-tegra186: Reserve and service a kernel watchdog".

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NVIDIA SAUCE patch; mainline is not affected]
Assisted-by: LLM
---
diff --git a/drivers/clocksource/timer-tegra186.c b/drivers/clocksource/timer-tegra186.c
index 36bb08825c5c..b0f349e70772 100644
--- a/drivers/clocksource/timer-tegra186.c
+++ b/drivers/clocksource/timer-tegra186.c
@@ -474,13 +474,6 @@ static int tegra186_timer_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	irq = err;
 
-	err = devm_request_irq(dev, irq, tegra186_timer_irq, 0,
-			       "tegra186-timer", tegra);
-	if (err < 0) {
-		dev_err(dev, "failed to request IRQ#%u: %d\n", irq, err);
-		return err;
-	}
-
 	/* create a watchdog using a preconfigured timer */
 	tegra->wdt = tegra186_wdt_create(tegra, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(tegra->wdt)) {
@@ -489,6 +482,13 @@ static int tegra186_timer_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return err;
 	}
 
+	err = devm_request_irq(dev, irq, tegra186_timer_irq, 0,
+			       "tegra186-timer", tegra);
+	if (err < 0) {
+		dev_err(dev, "failed to request IRQ#%u: %d\n", irq, err);
+		return err;
+	}
+
 	err = tegra186_timer_tsc_init(tegra);
 	if (err < 0) {
 		dev_err(dev, "failed to register TSC counter: %d\n", err);
